IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), Part III, ss 68-70: severe disablement allowance (ss 68, 69: blank in this text)
-- and carer's allowance (s 70). LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Plain-text rendering by a converter script, not the official text.
-- BAR POLARITY: a "shall not be entitled" function answers "is the person barred?": JUST TRUE = the text says not entitled;
-- JUST FALSE = the text says no bar (a failed "if", an "unless" met); NOTHING = the rule is silent on the case.

§ `Part III -- Non-Contributory Benefits: carer's allowance`

§§ `s 70 -- Carer's allowance`

-- s 70(2): "severely disabled person" MEANS a person in respect of whom there is payable one of the listed payments (and, last, "such other payment ... as may be prescribed").
-- src:1992 | (2) In this section, “severely disabled person” means a person in respect of whom there is payable either an attendance allowance or a disability living allowance by virtue of entitlement to the care component at the highest or middle rate or personal independence payment by virtue of entitlement to the daily living component at the standard or enhanced rate or armed forces independence payment under the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2011 (S.I. 2011/517) or adult disability payment by virtue of entitlement to the daily living component at the standard or enhanced rate or child disability payment by virtue of entitlement to the care component at the middle or highest rate or Scottish adult disability living allowance by virtue of entitlement to the care component at the middle or highest rate or pension age disability payment or such other payment out of public funds on account of his need for attendance as may be prescribed.
@ref s 70(2) (src:1992)
DECLARE `s 70(2) Payment in respect of the person cared for` IS ONE OF
    `s 70(2) attendance allowance`
    `s 70(2) disability living allowance, care component at the highest rate`
    `s 70(2) disability living allowance, care component at the middle rate`
    `s 70(2) personal independence payment, daily living component at the standard rate`
    `s 70(2) personal independence payment, daily living component at the enhanced rate`
    `s 70(2) armed forces independence payment under the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2011`
    `s 70(2) adult disability payment, daily living component at the standard rate`
    `s 70(2) adult disability payment, daily living component at the enhanced rate`
    `s 70(2) child disability payment, care component at the middle rate`
    `s 70(2) child disability payment, care component at the highest rate`
    `s 70(2) Scottish adult disability living allowance, care component at the middle rate`
    `s 70(2) Scottish adult disability living allowance, care component at the highest rate`
    `s 70(2) pension age disability payment`
    `s 70(2) such other payment out of public funds on account of his need for attendance`
    `s 70(2) a payment the definition does not name`    -- for example the care component of disability living allowance at the lowest rate

-- src:1992 | (2) In this section, “severely disabled person” means a person in respect of whom there is payable either an attendance allowance or a disability living allowance by virtue of entitlement to the care component at the highest or middle rate or personal independence payment by virtue of entitlement to the daily living component at the standard or enhanced rate or armed forces independence payment under the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2011 (S.I. 2011/517) or adult disability payment by virtue of entitlement to the daily living component at the standard or enhanced rate or child disability payment by virtue of entitlement to the care component at the middle or highest rate or Scottish adult disability living allowance by virtue of entitlement to the care component at the middle or highest rate or pension age disability payment or such other payment out of public funds on account of his need for attendance as may be prescribed.
@ref s 70(2) (src:1992)
GIVEN payment IS A `s 70(2) Payment in respect of the person cared for`
      `the payment is one prescribed as such a payment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70(2) the person cared for is a severely disabled person` MEANS
    CONSIDER payment
    WHEN `s 70(2) attendance allowance` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 70(2) disability living allowance, care component at the highest rate` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 70(2) disability living allowance, care component at the middle rate` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 70(2) personal independence payment, daily living component at the standard rate` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 70(2) personal independence payment, daily living component at the enhanced rate` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 70(2) armed forces independence payment under the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2011` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 70(2) adult disability payment, daily living component at the standard rate` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 70(2) adult disability payment, daily living component at the enhanced rate` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 70(2) child disability payment, care component at the middle rate` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 70(2) child disability payment, care component at the highest rate` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 70(2) Scottish adult disability living allowance, care component at the middle rate` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 70(2) Scottish adult disability living allowance, care component at the highest rate` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 70(2) pension age disability payment` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 70(2) such other payment out of public funds on account of his need for attendance` THEN
        CONSIDER `the payment is one prescribed as such a payment`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "as may be prescribed"; the regulations are not among the sources
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“severely disabled person” means a person in respect of whom there is payable" a listed payment or one prescribed
    WHEN `s 70(2) a payment the definition does not name` THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“severely disabled person” means a person in respect of whom there is payable either"

-- s 70(1): "A person shall be entitled to a carer's allowance for any day on which he is engaged in caring for a severely disabled person if" (a), (b) and (c).
-- (c) is "such relative of his as may be prescribed or a person of any such other description as may be prescribed": regulations outside the sources, so an input.
-- src:1984 | (1) A person shall be entitled to a carer’s allowance for any day on which he is engaged in caring for a severely disabled person if—
-- src:1985 | (a) he is regularly and substantially engaged in caring for that person;
-- src:1986 | (b) he is not gainfully employed; and
-- src:1987 | (c) the severely disabled person is either such relative of his as may be prescribed or a person of any such other description as may be prescribed.
@ref s 70(1) (src:1984-1987)
GIVEN `the person is engaged in caring for a severely disabled person on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is regularly and substantially engaged in caring for that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is gainfully employed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the severely disabled person is such a relative of his, or a person of such another description, as may be prescribed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70(1) the person is entitled to a carer's allowance for the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is engaged in caring for a severely disabled person on the day`) THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for any day on which he is engaged in caring for a severely disabled person if"
        IF NOT (`the person is regularly and substantially engaged in caring for that person`) THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if (a) he is regularly and substantially engaged in caring for that person"
        IF `the person is gainfully employed` THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if ... (b) he is not gainfully employed"
        IF `the severely disabled person is such a relative of his, or a person of such another description, as may be prescribed` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if ... (c) the severely disabled person is either such relative of his as may be prescribed or a person of any such other description as may be prescribed"
        IF `the severely disabled person is such a relative of his, or a person of such another description, as may be prescribed` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the relatives and descriptions are prescribed by regulations that are not among the sources

-- The days of the week in this Part: "week" here is Sunday to Saturday (s 122(1), the core's first Week convention). 5 January 2025 was a Sunday.
-- The number of days from the Sunday on or before the day: 0 for Sunday ... 6 for Saturday.
-- src:1988 | (1A) A person who was entitled to an allowance under this section immediately before the death of the severely disabled person referred to in subsection (1) shall continue to be entitled to it, even though he is no longer engaged in caring for a severely disabled person (and the requirements of subsection (1)(a) and (c) are not satisfied), until—
-- src:1989 | (a) the end of the week in which he ceases to satisfy any other requirement as to entitlement to the allowance; or
-- src:1990 | (b) the expiry of the period of eight weeks beginning with the Sunday following the death (or beginning with the date of death if the death occurred on Sunday),
-- src:1991 | whichever occurs first.
@ref s 70(1A) (src:1988-1991)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 70(1A) the days since the last Sunday` MEANS
    ((Day day) MINUS (Day (Date 5 1 2025))) MODULO 7

-- s 70(1A): after the severely disabled person's death a person entitled immediately before it "shall continue to be entitled ... until" the earlier of
-- (a) the end of the week in which he ceases to satisfy any other requirement as to entitlement; (b) the expiry of the period of eight weeks beginning with the Sunday following the death
-- (or beginning with the date of death if the death occurred on Sunday). "until": the entitlement is taken to run through the last day named (fork F3 in NOTES.md).
-- src:1988 | (1A) A person who was entitled to an allowance under this section immediately before the death of the severely disabled person referred to in subsection (1) shall continue to be entitled to it, even though he is no longer engaged in caring for a severely disabled person (and the requirements of subsection (1)(a) and (c) are not satisfied), until—
-- src:1989 | (a) the end of the week in which he ceases to satisfy any other requirement as to entitlement to the allowance; or
-- src:1990 | (b) the expiry of the period of eight weeks beginning with the Sunday following the death (or beginning with the date of death if the death occurred on Sunday),
-- src:1991 | whichever occurs first.
@ref s 70(1A) (src:1988-1991)
GIVEN `the person was entitled to a carer's allowance immediately before the death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the death` IS A DATE
      `the day on which he first ceases to satisfy any other requirement as to entitlement` IS A MAYBE DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70(1A) the person continues to be entitled to a carer's allowance for the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person was entitled to a carer's allowance immediately before the death`) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who was entitled to an allowance under this section immediately before the death"
        IF day LESS THAN `the date of the death` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the continuation runs from the death; before it subsection (1) governs
        IF day AT MOST `the last day of continued entitlement` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall continue to be entitled to it ... until" the end of the week or the expiry of the eight weeks, whichever occurs first
    WHERE
        `the first Sunday on or after the death` MEANS
            IF   (`s 70(1A) the days since the last Sunday` `the date of the death`) EQUALS 0
            THEN `the date of the death`
            ELSE `the date of the death` PLUS (7 MINUS (`s 70(1A) the days since the last Sunday` `the date of the death`))
        `the last day of the eight weeks` MEANS `the first Sunday on or after the death` PLUS 55
        `the last day of the continued entitlement under paragraph (a)` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day on which he first ceases to satisfy any other requirement as to entitlement`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST `the last day of the eight weeks`
            WHEN JUST ceased THEN JUST (ceased PLUS (6 MINUS (`s 70(1A) the days since the last Sunday` ceased)))
        `the last day of continued entitlement` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the last day of the continued entitlement under paragraph (a)`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the last day of the eight weeks`
            WHEN JUST endOfWeek THEN IF endOfWeek LESS THAN `the last day of the eight weeks` THEN endOfWeek ELSE `the last day of the eight weeks`

-- s 70(3): "A person shall not be entitled to an allowance under this section if he is under the age of 16 or receiving full-time education."
-- K2: s 173(a) says "under 16" means has not attained 16, and the answer is an input.
-- src:1993 | (3) A person shall not be entitled to an allowance under this section if he is under the age of 16 or receiving full-time education.
@ref s 70(3) (src:1993)
GIVEN `s 173(a) the person is under 16` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is receiving full-time education` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70(3) the person is barred from a carer's allowance by age or education` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 173(a) the person is under 16` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE    -- the text says no (a flat negative): "shall not be entitled to an allowance under this section if he is under the age of 16"
        IF `the person is receiving full-time education` THEN JUST TRUE    -- the text says no (a flat negative): "or receiving full-time education"
        IF `s 173(a) the person is under 16` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if he is under the age of 16 or receiving full-time education" does not apply to a person who is neither
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer to s 173(a) is not supplied

-- s 70(4): "shall not be entitled ... unless he satisfies prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain."
-- src:1994 | (4) A person shall not be entitled to an allowance under this section unless he satisfies prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain.
@ref s 70(4) (src:1994)
GIVEN `the person satisfies the prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70(4) the person is barred from a carer's allowance by the residence and presence conditions` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person satisfies the prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the conditions are prescribed by regulations that are not among the sources
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be entitled to an allowance under this section unless he satisfies prescribed conditions"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE    -- the text says no (a flat negative with "unless" not met): "shall not be entitled to an allowance under this section unless he satisfies prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain"

-- s 70(4A): the Regulations (EC) No 1408/71 and 883/2004: not entitled "for a period unless during that period the United Kingdom is competent".
-- src:1995 | (4A) A person to whom either Regulation (EC) No 1408/71 or Regulation (EC) No 883/2004 applies shall not be entitled to an allowance under this section for a period unless during that period the United Kingdom is competent for payment of sickness benefits in cash to the person for the purposes of Chapter 1 of Title III of the Regulation in question.
@ref s 70(4A) (src:1995)
GIVEN `Regulation (EC) No 1408/71 or Regulation (EC) No 883/2004 applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the United Kingdom is competent for payment of sickness benefits in cash to the person during the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70(4A) the person is barred from a carer's allowance for the period by the Regulations` MEANS
    IF   NOT (`Regulation (EC) No 1408/71 or Regulation (EC) No 883/2004 applies to the person`)
    THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar applies only to "A person to whom either Regulation ... applies"
    ELSE IF `the United Kingdom is competent for payment of sickness benefits in cash to the person during the period`
         THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be entitled to an allowance under this section for a period unless during that period the United Kingdom is competent"
         ELSE JUST TRUE    -- the text says no (a flat negative with "unless" not met): "shall not be entitled to an allowance under this section for a period unless"

-- s 70(7): "No person shall be entitled for the same day to (a) more than one allowance under this section; or (b) both an allowance under this section and carer support payment."
-- src:1998 | (7) No person shall be entitled for the same day to—
-- src:1999 | (a) more than one allowance under this section; or
-- src:2000 | (b) both an allowance under this section and carer support payment.
@ref s 70(7) (src:1998-2000)
GIVEN `the number of allowances under this section the person would be entitled to for the day` IS A NUMBER
      `the person would be entitled to carer support payment for the day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70(7) the person is barred from a further allowance for the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of allowances under this section the person would be entitled to for the day` GREATER THAN 1 THEN JUST TRUE    -- the text says no (a flat negative): "No person shall be entitled for the same day to (a) more than one allowance under this section"
        IF (`the number of allowances under this section the person would be entitled to for the day` AT LEAST 1) AND `the person would be entitled to carer support payment for the day` THEN JUST TRUE    -- the text says no (a flat negative): "No person shall be entitled for the same day to ... (b) both an allowance under this section and carer support payment"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar concerns "more than one allowance" or "both" an allowance and carer support payment

-- s 70(7ZA): where two or more persons would have a relevant entitlement for the same day for the same severely disabled person, one only shall have it:
-- (a) as they may jointly elect in the prescribed manner; or (b) in default of an election, as the Secretary of State determines in the Secretary of State's discretion.
-- JUST TRUE for the election/determination = this person; JUST FALSE = another person; NOTHING = no election and no determination yet (a judgment the Act hands to the Secretary of State).
-- src:2001 | (7ZA) Where, apart from this subsection, two or more persons would have a relevant entitlement for the same day in respect of the same severely disabled person, one of them only shall have that entitlement and that shall be such one of them—
-- src:2002 | (a) as they may jointly elect in the prescribed manner; or
-- src:2003 | (b) as may, in default of such an election, be determined by the Secretary of State in the Secretary of State’s discretion.
@ref s 70(7ZA) (src:2001-2003)
GIVEN `the number of persons who would have a relevant entitlement for the day in respect of the same severely disabled person` IS A NUMBER
      `the persons jointly elected this person in the prescribed manner` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State determined that this person shall have the entitlement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70(7ZA) the person is the one who has the relevant entitlement for the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of persons who would have a relevant entitlement for the day in respect of the same severely disabled person` LESS THAN 2 THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the rule applies "Where ... two or more persons would have a relevant entitlement"
        IF `the persons jointly elected this person in the prescribed manner` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the persons jointly elected this person in the prescribed manner` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "one of them only shall have that entitlement" and the joint election named another
        IF `the Secretary of State determined that this person shall have the entitlement` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the Secretary of State determined that this person shall have the entitlement` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "one of them only shall have that entitlement" and the determination named another
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the election is "in the prescribed manner" and the default determination is "in the Secretary of State's discretion"

-- s 70(7ZB): "Subsection (7ZC) applies where a person (A)" (a) has or would have an entitlement to carer support payment (disregarding reg 5(3)), or (b) has or would have an entitlement to carer's allowance decided by the Scottish Ministers.
-- src:2004 | (7ZB) Subsection (7ZC) applies where a person (A)—
-- src:2005 | (a) (disregarding the effect of regulation 5(3) of the Carer’s Assistance (Carer Support Payment) (Scotland) Regulations 2023) has, or would have, an entitlement to carer support payment; or
-- src:2006 | (b) has, or would have, an entitlement to carer’s allowance in respect of which the Scottish Ministers have the power to make decisions,
-- src:2007 | for a day in respect of a severely disabled person.
@ref s 70(7ZB) (src:2004-2007)
GIVEN `A has or would have an entitlement to carer support payment, disregarding the effect of regulation 5(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `A has or would have an entitlement to carer's allowance in respect of which the Scottish Ministers have the power to make decisions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70(7ZB) subsection (7ZC) applies` MEANS
    IF   `A has or would have an entitlement to carer support payment, disregarding the effect of regulation 5(3)`
      OR `A has or would have an entitlement to carer's allowance in respect of which the Scottish Ministers have the power to make decisions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (7ZC) applies where a person (A)" is within (a) or (b); the text does not say it applies only then

-- s 70(7ZC): "Another person (B) shall not have a relevant entitlement for the same day ... unless (a) A and B jointly elect ... or (b) in default of such an election, the Secretary of State is satisfied, following consultation with the Scottish Ministers, that (i) and (ii)."
-- The Secretary of State's satisfaction is a judgment the Act hands to that official, so it is an input.
-- src:2008 | (7ZC) Another person (B) shall not have a relevant entitlement for the same day in respect of the same severely disabled person unless—
-- src:2009 | (a) A and B jointly elect in the prescribed manner that B shall have the relevant entitlement (and that A shall not have an entitlement mentioned in subsection (7ZB)) for that day in respect of that severely disabled person; or
-- src:2010 | (b) in default of such an election, the Secretary of State is satisfied, following consultation with the Scottish Ministers, that—
-- src:2011 | (i) the Scottish Ministers have decided, or will decide, that A shall not have an entitlement mentioned in subsection (7ZB); and
-- src:2012 | (ii) B shall have the relevant entitlement,
-- src:2013 | for that day in respect of that severely disabled person.
@ref s 70(7ZC) (src:2008-2013)
GIVEN `subsection (7ZC) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `A and B jointly elect in the prescribed manner that B shall have the relevant entitlement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in default of an election the Secretary of State is satisfied, following consultation with the Scottish Ministers, that the Scottish Ministers have decided or will decide that A shall not have the entitlement and that B shall have the relevant entitlement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70(7ZC) the other person B is barred from a relevant entitlement for the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`subsection (7ZC) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is for where subsection (7ZC) applies under (7ZB)
        IF `A and B jointly elect in the prescribed manner that B shall have the relevant entitlement` THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not have a relevant entitlement for the same day ... unless (a) A and B jointly elect"
        IF `in default of an election the Secretary of State is satisfied, following consultation with the Scottish Ministers, that the Scottish Ministers have decided or will decide that A shall not have the entitlement and that B shall have the relevant entitlement` THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless ... (b) in default of such an election, the Secretary of State is satisfied"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE    -- the text says no (a flat negative with "unless" not met): "Another person (B) shall not have a relevant entitlement for the same day in respect of the same severely disabled person unless"

-- s 70(7A): a person has a "relevant entitlement" if (a) entitled to a carer's allowance decided by the Secretary of State, or (b) entitled under s 12 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 to the universal credit carer element.
-- src:2014 | (7A) For the purposes of subsections (7ZA) and (7ZC) a person has a “relevant entitlement” if—
-- src:2015 | (a) the person is entitled to a carer’s allowance in respect of which the Secretary of State has the power to make decisions , or
-- src:2016 | (b) the person is entitled under section 12 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 to the inclusion in an award of universal credit of an amount in respect of the fact that the person has regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person.
@ref s 70(7A) (src:2014-2016)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to a carer's allowance in respect of which the Secretary of State has the power to make decisions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is entitled under section 12 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 to the inclusion in an award of universal credit of an amount for regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70(7A) the person has a relevant entitlement` MEANS
    IF   `the person is entitled to a carer's allowance in respect of which the Secretary of State has the power to make decisions`
      OR `the person is entitled under section 12 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 to the inclusion in an award of universal credit of an amount for regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person has a “relevant entitlement” if"

-- s 70(7B): "carer support payment" means carer's assistance, the carer support payment component of carer support given in accordance with the 2023 Regulations.
-- src:2017 | (7B) In subsections (7) and (7ZB), “carer support payment” means carer’s assistance the carer support payment component of carer support given in accordance with the Carer’s Assistance (Carer Support Payment) (Scotland) Regulations 2023.
@ref s 70(7B) (src:2017)
GIVEN `it is the carer support payment component of carer's assistance given in accordance with the Carer's Assistance (Carer Support Payment) (Scotland) Regulations 2023` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70(7B) the payment is carer support payment` MEANS
    IF   `it is the carer support payment component of carer's assistance given in accordance with the Carer's Assistance (Carer Support Payment) (Scotland) Regulations 2023`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“carer support payment” means"

-- s 70(8): regulations may prescribe when a person is treated as engaged, regularly and substantially engaged, gainfully employed or in full-time education (a regulation-making power; inert, machinery).

-- s 70(9): "A carer's allowance shall be payable at the weekly rate specified in Schedule 4, Part III, paragraph 4." The Schedule 4 table is omitted from this text, so the rate is an input.
-- src:2019 | (9) A carer’s allowance shall be payable at the weekly rate specified in Schedule 4, Part III, paragraph 4.
@ref s 70(9) (src:2019)
GIVEN `sch 4 pt III para 4 the weekly rate of carer's allowance in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 70(9) the weekly rate of a carer's allowance in pounds` MEANS
    `sch 4 pt III para 4 the weekly rate of carer's allowance in pounds`    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) if the Schedule 4 figure is not supplied
